#: ../command-line.rst:149
msgid "Super administrator password"
msgstr ""

#: ../command-line.rst:153
msgid "The super administrator password is normally changed from **My account**, then **My information**, or from the :ref:`advanced configuration <advanced_config>` page. Both require to be logged in, which is of little help the day the password is lost: the super administrator is not a member, so it cannot use the *forgotten password* form either."
msgstr ""

#: ../command-line.rst:155
msgid "This command is the way back in. It runs on the machine hosting Galette, and that access stands as the authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../command-line.rst:175
msgid "There is no option to pass the password with: it is only ever read from a hidden prompt, so that it does not end up in your shell history nor in the process list of the machine. It is asked twice, and the two answers must match."
msgstr ""

#: ../command-line.rst:194
msgid "The login is displayed so you know which account you just changed, but the command does not touch it. Change it from **My account**, then **My information**, as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../command-line.rst:196
msgid "The new password must satisfy the :ref:`password rules <password_rules>` of your instance, exactly as it would from the web interface."
msgstr ""

